/-
# Faithful irreducible representations of soluble groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 9.12)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 9.12 (D. I. Zaitsev): is there a soluble
group with the following properties: torsion-free of finite rank, not finitely generated, and having
a faithful irreducible representation over a finite field?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.OrderOfElement
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.Solvable
public import Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Basic
public import Mathlib.RepresentationTheory.Irreducible
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TorsionFreeFiniteRankFaithfulIrreducibleKourovka9Problem12Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 9.12 (D. I.
Zaitsev). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700547 (`KOU-9.12`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

Torsion-free is `∀ g, g ≠ 1 → ¬ IsOfFinOrder g`. "Finite rank" in this (soluble) context is finite
Prüfer (special) rank, the 1.23 entry's `HasFiniteRank`: there is `r` such that every finitely
generated subgroup is generated by at most `r` elements. A representation over a finite field `k` is
a `Representation k G V` on a `k`-vector space of any dimension; faithful is injective, irreducible
is Mathlib's `Representation.IsIrreducible` (`V ≠ 0` with no `G`-invariant subspaces other than
`0` and `V`).
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.LocallyFiniteSimpleFiniteRankKourovka1Problem23Wanted

/-- Kourovka 9.12 (D. I. Zaitsev): there is a soluble group `G`, torsion-free, of finite rank
(`HasFiniteRank`, from the 1.23 entry) and not finitely generated, with a faithful irreducible
representation over a finite field `k`: an injective representation `ρ` on a non-zero `k`-vector
space `V` (of any dimension) with no `G`-invariant subspaces other than `0` and `V`. -/
def existsTorsionFreeFiniteRankFaithfulIrreducible : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), Group.IsSolvable G ∧ (∀ g : G, g ≠ 1 → ¬ IsOfFinOrder g) ∧
    HasFiniteRank G ∧ ¬ Group.FG G ∧
    ∃ (k : Type) (_ : Field k) (_ : Finite k) (V : Type) (_ : AddCommGroup V) (_ : Module k V)
      (ρ : Representation k G V), Function.Injective ρ ∧ ρ.IsIrreducible

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 9.12 "Yes, there is", citing Tushev's paper on
irreducible representations of locally polycyclic groups over an absolute field: some soluble
torsion-free group of finite rank that is not finitely generated has a faithful irreducible
representation over a finite field. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved
Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of
Solved Problems, Problem 9.12 (D. I. Zaitsev); resolution: A. V. Tushev, Irreducible representations
of locally polycyclic groups over an absolute field, Ukrainian Math. J. 42 (1990), 1233-1238,
Kourovka Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 9.12: Yes, there is,
https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01057395.
-/
public theorem_wanted existsTorsionFreeFiniteRankFaithfulIrreducible_holds :
    existsTorsionFreeFiniteRankFaithfulIrreducible

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.TorsionFreeFiniteRankFaithfulIrreducibleKourovka9Problem12Wanted
